15678408,2025-09-02,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Took or threatened to take negative or legal action,Sued you without properly notifying you of lawsuit,"In XXXX, I was sued for a debt in XXXX XXXX, Florida. In XX/XX/XXXX, the case was disposed after the court approved a stipulation. I never heard from the creditor or collector again. No motion was filed to reopen the case, and I believed it was over. 

Over a year later, in XX/XX/XXXX, the collector obtained a final judgment against me without my knowledge. They never served me or provided proper notice. They mailed documents to an old address, even though my correct address was available on my Florida drivers license issued in XXXX and was a matter of public record. They made no effort to confirm my location through the DMV, skip tracing, or any reasonable means. I had no notice of this judgment until XX/XX/XXXX, more than ten years later. 

This was done through extrinsic fraud. The collector reused paperwork from the closed case to get a judgment without filing new motions or giving me a chance to respond. There were no collection efforts for more than ten years. Then in XXXX, they suddenly used the old judgment to issue subpoenas, contact third parties, and disclose my personal and confidential information in court filings without redaction. This included my full address and landlords name, which were placed into the public record in violation of Floridas confidentiality rules. 

Their actions violated federal and state collection laws, including : Misrepresenting the legal status of a debt by enforcing a void and time-barred judgment. 

Contacting third parties ( landlords and others ) in an attempt to collect, which is prohibited by the FDCPA. 

Harassing me and causing me to lose my place of living in XXXX because of their unlawful contacts. 

I am requesting that the CFPB investigate these violations and hold the collector accountable. I want the judgment removed as it was obtained without jurisdiction or notice, and I want the third-party contacts and improper use of my confidential information to be addressed.",,"Surf Consultants, Inc.",FL,33189,,Web,2025-09-02,Closed with explanation,Yes
